<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Túcume</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Túcume is an archaeological complex in the Lambayeque valley of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a>, with 26 large adobe pyramids around a rocky hill. Built from around 1100 as the Late Sicán centre after <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/batan-grande">Batán Grande</a> was abandoned, it was later occupied by the Chimú and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inca-empire">Incas</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thor">Thor</a> Heyerdahl led excavations there between 1988 and 1994.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/tucume.jpg" alt="Túcume" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bernard Gagnon · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Site_of_T%C3%BAcume_02.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
